{# DeD Downed (spec 19.2 / 20, S347 + S351): what one victorious enemy does now that the player's side is beaten and downed.
   Context from DeDDowned.dll: victorId (FormID), targets (list of {key, id, name, player}), location (text),
   offer (object: an outcome key -> true when the user allows it and its module is installed; offer.rob = ask the
   robbery question), again (true = "keep going" re-ask), done (what this victor already did, text).
   Read by question id and option key: target -> a targets[].key; action -> an offered key (all probabilities kept,
   DeDDowned.dll weights and rolls them, spec D-A66); rob -> yes / no (noul). LLM-facing; DRAFT at the user's pen. #}
{% set victor = formid_to_uuid(victorId) %}

[ state victor ]
    ### {{ decnpc(victor).name }}
    {{ render_character_profile("short_inline", victor) }}
[ end state ]

[ state downed ]
    {{ decnpc(victor).name }}'s side has just won a fight{% if location != "" %} at {{ location }}{% endif %}. These people from the losing side lie beaten and helpless nearby:
    {% for t in targets %}
    - {{ t.key }}: {{ t.name }}{% if t.player %} (the player){% endif %}: {{ render_character_profile("short_inline", formid_to_uuid(t.id)) }}
    {% endfor %}
    {% if again %}
    {{ decnpc(victor).name }} has already: {{ done }}.
    {% endif %}
[ end state ]

[ question target choice ]
    Which of the people in `downed` does {{ decnpc(victor).name }} turn to{% if again %} next{% endif %}? Judge from `victor`: who they want, resent or have business with.
    [ criteria ]
    {% for t in targets %}{{ t.key }}: {{ t.name }}
    {% endfor %}
    [ end criteria ]
[ end question ]

[ question action choice ]
    What does {{ decnpc(victor).name }} do to that person {% if again %}next, after what they have already done{% else %}now{% endif %}, true to their character in `victor` (an enemy who just won, not a friend)?
    [ criteria ]
    {% if offer.sex %}sex: takes them sexually while they are helpless
    {% endif %}{% if offer.threaten %}threaten: threatens, taunts and humiliates them, then leaves them
    {% endif %}{% if offer.strip %}strip: strips them of their clothes and armour and leaves them bare
    {% endif %}{% if offer.tattoo %}tattoo: marks their skin with a tattoo as a trophy or a humiliation
    {% endif %}{% if offer.makeup %}makeup: paints their face to mock and humiliate them
    {% endif %}{% if offer.execute %}execute: kills them where they lie
    {% endif %}leave: {% if again %}has had enough and leaves them{% else %}leaves them where they lie{% endif %}
    [ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
{% if offer.rob %}

[ question rob noul ]
    Does {{ decnpc(victor).name }} also go through that person's belongings and take what they want, true to their character in `victor`?
[ end question ]
{% endif %}
